ible. Chains and locks lose their hold, dissolving effortlessly under the wizards touch.<br /> <br /> 1) Find Exits<br /> 2) Open Locks<br /> 3) Escape From Restraints<br /> 4) Escape From Prisons<br /> 5) Becoming Intangible<br /> <br /> Control<br /> <br /> Power: Energy / Telekinesis<br /> <br /> Knowledge: Evocation - Harnessing the forces of the spiritual realm.<br /> <br /> Description: The Power of Control enables a wizard to command powerful forces. Through evocation, the practitioner can manipulate energy and bend it to their will. This understanding arises from recognizing that spiritual entities are themselves embodiments of force and possess the capacity to shape and impact the physical world.<br /> <br /> 1) Quick Reactions<br /> 2) Bonus to Physical Abilities<br /> 3) Influencing Physical Outcomes<br /> 4) Moving Objects<br /> 5) Controlling Natural Forces<br /> <br /> Restoration<br /> <br /> Power: Renewal / Healing<br /> <br /> Knowledge: Forgiveness - Liberating from suffering caused by transgressions.<br /> <br /> Description: The Power of Restoration holds the gift of healing. It grants the ability to alleviate pain, cure diseases, and bring renewal to the afflicted. This power emerges from the understanding of Forgiveness, recognizing that suffering often stems from transgressions. By embracing forgiveness, a wizard becomes a conduit for healing and restoration.<br /> <br /> 1) Sense illness<br /> 2) Relieve Pain<br /> 3) Protection from Disease<br /> 4) Heal Sickness / Damage<br /> 5) Resurrection<br /> <br /> Vanishing<br /> <br /> Power: Stealth / Invisibility<br /> <br /> Knowledge: Misdirection - Manipulating attention and perception.<br /> <br /> Description: The Power of Vanishing encompasses the art of Misdirection. It allows a wizard to control focus and attention, rendering themselves unseen and secrets concealed. Meticulous study and practice grant the ability to achieve complete invisibility as the wizard manipulates perception and directs attention elsewhere.<br /> <br /> 1) Safeguard Secrets<br /> 2) See in The Dark<br /> 3) Stealth<br /> 4) Disguise<br /> 5) Invisibility<br /> <br /> Travel<br /> <br /> Power: Direction / Teleportation<br /> <br /> Knowledge: Unity - Dissolving the illusion of separation.<br /> <br /> Description: The Power of Travel operates on the understanding that all separation is illusory. By harnessing this power, a wizard can navigate without traditional directions and locate objects or places that are lost or hidden. A skilled practitioner can transcend distance, stepping from one location to any desired destination.<br /> <br /> 1) Locate Lost Objects<br /> 2) Find Directions<br /> 3) See at a Distance<br /> 4) Teleport Objects<br /> 5) Make a Portal<br /> <br /> Transformation<br /> <br /> Power: Developing / Shapeshifting<br /> <br /> Knowledge: Personification - Authoring ones own identity.<br /> <br /> Description: The Power of Transformation allows a wizard to assume the form and essence of another being, whether it be an abstract concept, an animal, or even a deity. The essence of this mastery lies in the understanding that one has the power to create and define their own identity, refusing to be shaped by external forces. The power of transformation can also be used to improve who you already are.<br /> <br /> 1) Sense Others Attributes<br /> 2) Bonus to Attributes<br /> 3) Developing Attributes<br /> 4) Shapeshifting<br /> 5) Transmutation<br /> <br /> Destruction<br /> <br /> Power: Curses / Annihilation<br /> <br /> Knowledge: Pragmatism - Dissolving the constructs of right and wrong<br /> <br /> Description: The Power of Destruction holds immense power that should be wielded with caution. It encompasses the ability to curse, annihilate, and disrupt the natural order. However, the utilization of this power draws one away from their true path and blurs the distinction between right and wrong.<br /> <br /> 1) Sense Black Magic<br /> 2) Protection from Curses<br /> 3) Curse Enemies<br /> 4) Cause Physical Damage<br /> 5) Kill &amp; Destroy<br /> <br /> Revelation<br /> <br /> Power: Visions / Rapture<br /> <br /> Knowledge: Above as Below - The symbiotic connection between gods, angels, and humanity.<br /> <br /> Description: The Power of Revelation unveils profound visions and grants enlightenment to the practitioner. It is rooted in the understanding of the symbiotic connection between gods, angels, and humanity. By tapping into this power, a wizard gains access to celestial knowledge, perceiving the intricate tapestry that binds all realms and entities together.<br /> <br /> 1) Sense Spirits<br /> 2) Speak with Spirits<br /> 3) Banish Spirits<br /> 4) Summon Spirits<br /> 5) Spirit Travel<br /> <br /> <br /> This system of magic can connect to occult themes, for interesting role playing.<br /> <br /> Each type of magic connects to one of the 12 signs of the Zodiac. And each Zodiac sign connects to one of 10 planets in Astrology. The 10 planets and 12 signs connect with the 22 Major Arcana of the Tarot.<br /> <br /> Control:<br /> Energy / Telekinesis<br /> (Aries / Emperor) + (Mars / Tower)<br /> <br /> Transformation:<br /> Developing / Shapeshifting<br /> (Taurus / Hierophant) + (Venus / Empress)<br /> <br /> Understanding:<br /> Wisdom / ESP<br /> (Libra / Justice) + (Venus / Empress)<br /> <br /> Revelation:<br /> Visions / Rapture<br /> (Pisces / High Priestess) + (Neptune /<br /> Hanged Man)<br /> <br /> Feeling:<br /> Empathy / Telepathy<br /> (Virgo / Hermit) + (Mercury / Magician)<br /> <br /> Influence:<br /> Charisma / Hypnotism<br /> (Leo / Strength) + (Sun / Sun)<br /> <br /> Penetration:<br /> Escape / Intangibility<br /> (Gemini / Lovers) + (Mercury / Magician)<br /> <br /> Travel:<br /> Direction / Teleportation<br /> (Sagittarius / Temperance) + (Jupiter /<br /> Wheel of Fortune)<br /> <br /> Production:<br /> Attraction / Creation<br /> (Capricorn / Devil) + (Saturn / World)<br /> <br /> Restoration:<br /> Renewal / Healing<br /> (Aquarius / Star) + (Uranus / Fool)<br /> <br /> Vanishing:<br /> Stealth / Invisibility<br /> (Cancer / Chariot) + (Moon / Moon)<br /> <br /> Destruction:<br /> Curses / Annihilation<br /> (Scorpio / Death) + (Pluto / Judgement)</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not think that the system that you present really fits in with Mage: The Ascension, but I must say that I like the way in which you weaved astrology and the Tarot into the magic system. That being said, I think that at the moment, the occult connections seem a bit superficial. There have been very few role-playing games about magic that have actually been accurate to real-world magical traditions. Even Nephilim and Kult present cosmologies that are vastly different from those modelled by many western occult traditions that those games were inspired by. In the case of your game, I think you can get away with inaccuracies, since the occult themes are intended to add flavor to the experience. I hope that you do the topic justice, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T00:52:50-07:00","id":1533739,"title":"","content":"If any of you wants to fiddle with the mechanics of the game, I'd suggest for you to buy the book Thaumatology from Gurps. It is beyond any doubt the absolute best source anywhere you could find about how to design the perfect (and I really mean the PERFECT) Magic system.<br /> <br /> You might wanna jump a few pages and go to the section about &quot;Open Magic&quot; (give me a moment to search the book up and find the proper name). There, it has the &quot;Realm Magic&quot; which is... A bit of a copy from Mage the Ascension. It also has &quot;Noun/Verb Magic&quot; which is a bit of a copy from... Is it Aberrant? I don't know, the other game from the same owners of MtA. Basically, in Realm Magic you divide everything into &quot;Realms&quot; (Spheres), in any amount that you so desire. Gurps has a system of character points, but don't worry, you don't need to learn Gurps to use this material. Just so you know that, for instance, let's say that 1000 points turns you an absolute archmaster in EVERYTHING Magic related, and you decided that your world will have 10 Spheres; than that means each Sphere will cost a total of 100 points to Master. If you decide that each of these &quot;Realms&quot; (Spheres) will have 5 levels, than each level will cost 20 points.<br /> <br /> That math was useful for me to design Minor and Alternative Spheres for my games. Oh yes, the book also tells you how to do the math for any number of levels. Do you want your Spheres to have just 3 levels each? Fine. You can do it. 7 levels? No problem. 10? As you wish.<br /> <br /> Oh, the Life Realm costs 100 CP (character points) total, 20 CP per level? Well then, the &quot;Plant Sub-Realm&quot; will only cost 1/5 of that, or 4 CPs per level. And so on.<br /> <br /> Then, you can just simply &quot;translate&quot; that back into the D10 system with some adjustments if you so wish.<br /> <br /> Not only that, but this book has so much more to offer. For instance, Gurps uses a system of &quot;Mama Level&quot;, which is something like the &quot;magical emanations&quot; of a place. Interestingly for us, that resembles somewhat the idea of Nodes. So, in this book they introduce the idea of &quot;cursed Mana&quot; levels and also &quot;chaotic Mana&quot; which can be used for dealing with Nodes in superb ways. And many, many more: &quot;Mana Organs&quot; for example is another wonderful idea, it relates to the idea of, trying to explain it in a resumed way, to &quot;harvest the organs of magic beings&quot; with some specific properties. It also holds many ideas on how to develop magic items and so.<br /> <br /> Gurps Fantasy is also another greating source, but while Gurps Thaumatology deals more with the design of game mechanics for magic systems, Gurps Fantasy deals with designing an interesting setting. But both are gold mines of ideas, which I use extensively.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T06:33:28-07:00","id":1533743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1529077-alternate-mage-rules?p=1533739#post1533739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If any of you wants to fiddle with the mechanics of the game, I'd suggest for you to buy the book Thaumatology from Gurps. It is beyond any doubt the absolute best source anywhere you could find about how to design the perfect (and I really mean the PERFECT) Magic system.<br /> <br /> You might wanna jump a few pages and go to the section about &quot;Open Magic&quot; (give me a moment to search the book up and find the proper name). There, it has the &quot;Realm Magic&quot; which is... A bit of a copy from Mage the Ascension.</div> </div> </div> </div>IN the 90s, Steve Jackson Games collaborated with White Wolf to provide a series of GURPS adaptations of World of Darkness games. They got four books out before relations between the companies collapsed into an epic mess. The last of those books was <i><b>GURPS Mage: the Ascension</b></i>. <br /> <br /> Realm Magic is \u201ca bit of a copy from Mage: the Ascension\u201d because it's the Magick system published in <i><b>GURPS Mage: the Ascension</b></i> with the serial numbers filed off. <br /> <br /> We now return you to your regular <b>Mage: the Ascension</b> content\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T07:20:22-07:00","id":1533745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1529077-alternate-mage-rules?p=1533743#post1533743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IN the 90s, Steve Jackson Games collaborated with White Wolf to provide a series of GURPS adaptations of World of Darkness games. They got four books out before relations between the companies collapsed into an epic mess. The last of those books was <i><b>GURPS Mage: the Ascension</b></i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I didn't mention Gurps MtA because not everybody is a fan of Gurps system. Gurps Thaumatology and Fantasy don't need previous knowledge of Gurps system to be used.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Realm Magic is \u201ca bit of a copy from Mage: the Ascension\u201d because it's the Magick system published in <i><b>GURPS Mage: the Ascension</b></i> with the serial numbers filed off.<br /> <br /> We now return you to your regular <b>Mage: the Ascension</b> content\u2026 </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. In the original Gurps MtA, it was just the regular 9 Spheres, previous to M20. In Thaumatology they vastly expanded the concept, allowing for the design of fully custom tailored &quot;Spheres&quot; (Realms). Throughout the last few years, they've published many variations. For instance and as a simple example, for their Dungeon Fantasy series, for typical &quot;Medieval Fantasy&quot; of the likes of D&amp;D, they have 8 &quot;Spheres&quot; for the &quot;Wizard Class&quot;, with things like Necromancy Realm and Divination Realm. And, magical healing is beyond the capabilities of Wizards (because it is the exclusive purview of &quot;the Gods&quot; - aka it's for the &quot;Cleric Class&quot;). <br /> <br /> I used this to design custom tailored Spheres for each individual group in MtA and also to design Sub Spheres. Necromancy Sphere, Alchemy Sphere, Space/Time Sphere, Biochemistry. All of those I use as &quot;Super-Spheres&quot;, and also an almost unlimited amount of Sub Spheres. I'm so used to it that my players already make their own sub Spheres. Plant Magic, Metamorphoses, Pyromancer, Cryomancer, Empath Mage, Telekinesis, those are all just a few examples of Sub Spheres I have been using.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T07:53:50-07:00","id":1533747,"title":"","content":"Regardless, that's a GURPS thing; and this isn't a GURPS forum. Let's not get too side tracked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-14T04:45:39-07:00","id":1534186,"title":"","content":"So, my ultimate goal is to make a new mage book with these rules. If anyone wants to work on that with me I have time and resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27363-street","name":"Street","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-14T15:44:29-07:00","id":1534215,"title":"","content":"What exactly do you mean by &quot;make a new mage book&quot; as the end goal?<br /> <br /> Publishing your own Mage branded book is illegal.<br /> <br /> Creating something that could be sold under the Storytellers Vault content agreement would be difficult without reducing how much change you're doing.<br /> <br /> Creating your own urban fantasy game about wizards that's heavily inspired by Mage is doable but probably don't have much of a market for the effort.<br /> <br /> Just making a &quot;book&quot; that's a fan-site with your rules and setting changes is the &quot;easiest&quot; but it's a bigger departure from your phrasing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-15T15:53:48-07:00","id":1534271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1529077-alternate-mage-rules?p=1534215#post1534215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly do you mean by &quot;make a new mage book&quot; as the end goal?<br /> <br /> Publishing your own Mage branded book is illegal.<br /> <br /> Creating something that could be sold under the Storytellers Vault content agreement would be difficult without reducing how much change you're doing.<br /> <br /> Creating your own urban fantasy game about wizards that's heavily inspired by Mage is doable but probably don't have much of a market for the effort.<br /> <br /> Just making a &quot;book&quot; that's a fan-site with your rules and setting changes is the &quot;easiest&quot; but it's a bigger departure from your phrasing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I realize there would be a copyright violation. But couldn't I get permission?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27363-street","name":"Street","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-15T16:27:51-07:00","id":1534274,"title":"","content":"More importantly than a copyright violation, it would be a trademark violation. Trademarks are much more likely to be defended hard in court.<br /> <br /> And while you can, in theory, ask, Paradox is going to say no.<br /> <br /> 1a) They license out the WoD games to other developers. So they're not going to say yes to a fan project for free when professionals have to pay them for the right to make Mage books.<br /> <br /> 1b) The exclusivity of those licensing deals is also important to their value. If anyone that asks, and pays, can make a Mage book, those doing so for a profit have to be concerned about failing to meet their margins because too many people are making Mage books for any one company to turn a profit from it.<br /> <br /> 2) Paradox already has two methods for fans to produce material: The Dark Pack fansite rules, and the Storyteller's Vault community content rules. Essentially, they've already said what the &quot;rules&quot; are for fans that want to make their own Mage books. They're just going to direct you to those and hold you to the rules provided.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}